ng H2O or H2 equivalents) must be explicitly stated to conserve mass/charge. Still, the pathway logic and environmental fit are sound.', 'This variant of reductive amination is plausible according to the literature (Muchowska et al., 2019) but, as written, is not mass and charge balanced (RDKit: unbalanced). The potential to balance with H2 or CO2 addition was noted but is not reflected in the network. Environmental context and mechanistic plausibility are high.', 'Lactic acid oxidation to pyruvate under cyanosulfidic conditions is literature-supported in principle (Ritson, 2021; rxn_008), but as written, rxn_008 is not atom/charge balanced and likely requires additional species (e.g., O2, CO2) per the balance check. Downstream amination remains unbalanced and problematic.', 'The hydrothermal oxidation of lactic acid to pyruvate (rxn_010) is speculative and lacks clear mass/charge balance (likely missing O2, CO2 or other small molecules). Downstream amination is still unbalanced.']\n\n============================================================\nAddress the above issues in your new network. Do NOT repeat the same mistakes.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"target_molecule\": \"L-Alanine\",\n  \"overall_strategy\": \"Construct a robust prebiotic synthesis network for L-Alanine starting from geochemically abundant feedstocks (CO2, H2, NH3, H2O) traversing hydrothermal and surface environments, converging at key intermediates (pyruvate, 2-aminopropanenitrile, L-serine), and connecting all main literature-demonstrated and chemically balanced pathways, with correct stoichiometric inclusion of all critical small molecules and byproducts per experimental precedent.\",\n  \"molecules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_001\",\n      \"formula\": \"CO2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"carbon dioxide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"carbon dioxide\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CO2/c2-1-3\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \