d.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Muchowska et al. (2019, Nature) demonstrated this stoichiometry as an experimentally valid net reaction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_004\",\n      \"name\": \"Fe\u00b2\u207a-catalyzed decarboxylation of oxaloacetate\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"ferrous iron (Fe\u00b2\u207a)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"343 K (70\u00b0C)\",\n        \"pressure\": \"moderate-high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Fe\u00b2\u207a\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"anoxic\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Fe\u00b2\u207a coordinates the \u03b2-keto acid moiety, lowering activation energy for loss of CO2 (decarboxylation).\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Directly supported by Muchowska et al. (2019, Nature); mass/charge balanced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_005\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyanosulfidic decarboxylation of oxaloacetate\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV light\", \"sulfur compounds (cyanosulfidic milieu)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-310 K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"wet-dry cycling, UV irradiation\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Photochemically/photo-catalyzed decarboxylation enabled by cyanosulfidic chemistry, releasing CO2 and forming pyruvate.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Ritson (2021, Science Advances) demonstrated prebiotic decarboxylation of oxaloacetate under surface cyanosulfidic conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_006\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyanosulfidic oxidation of lactic acid to pyruvate (with H2 as byproduct)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_007\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"environme