al conversion of lactic acid to L-serine\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_007\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_011\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV light\", \"clay minerals (montmorillonite)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-340 K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"montmorillonite\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"UV irradiation\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Oxidative amination; photoredox conversion of \u03b1-hydroxy acid to \u03b1-amino acid supported by clay-mediated photochemistry.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Speculative as no direct evidence for surface formation of serine from lactic acid, but analogous chemistry plausible (Patel et al., 2015).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pathways\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"name\": \"Direct cyanosulfidic aminonitrile hydrolysis (surface)\",\n      \"description\": \"2-Aminopropanenitrile forms in surface cyanosulfidic chemistry and hydrolyzes under wet-dry cycles directly to L-Alanine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_009\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrothermal CO2 fixation \u2192 pyruvate \u2192 iron-catalyzed reductive amination (hydrated variant)\",\n      \"description\": \"CO2 and H2 undergo iron/awaruite-catalyzed reduction to pyruvate, then iron-catalyzed reductive amination with hydroxylamine and water yields L-Alanine.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"name\": \"Fischer-Tropsch CO2 fixation \u2192 pyruvate \u2192 iron-catalyzed reductive amination (dehydration variant)\",\n      \"description\": \"Hydrothermal CO2/H2 reduced to pyruvate, then pyruvate + hydroxylamine (net dehydration) iron-catalyzed conversion to L-Alanine.\",\n      \"reaction_